---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import "../../styles/global.css";
---

<Docs title="Config">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-10">
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Config</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">Workspace-local configuration via <code>.craig/config.json</code>.</p>

    <p>All config is optional. Craig works out of the box with defaults.</p>

    <pre><code>{`{
  "runners": {
    "codex":  { "enabled": true },
    "cursor": { "enabled": true },
    "claude": { "enabled": false }
  },
  "checks": {
    "commands": ["pnpm test", "pnpm typecheck", "pnpm lint"]
  },
  "github": {
    "mergeMethod": "squash",
    "watchIntervalSeconds": 5
  }
}`}</code></pre>

    <h2>runners</h2>
    <p>
      Controls which agent runners are available in this workspace. Set <code>enabled: false</code> to hide a runner,
      or provide a custom <code>path</code> to override the binary location. See <a href="/docs/runners">Runners</a> for full details.
    </p>

    <h2>checks.commands</h2>
    <p>
      Commands run by <code>craig task check &lt;id&gt;</code>. Typically your test, typecheck, and lint scripts.
      Output is shown in the Review inspector panel.
    </p>

    <h2>github.mergeMethod</h2>
    <p>
      Merge strategy used when merging PRs via Craig. Accepts <code>squash</code>, <code>merge</code>, or <code>rebase</code>.
      Defaults to <code>squash</code>.
    </p>

    <h2>github.watchIntervalSeconds</h2>
    <p>
      How often Craig polls GitHub for PR check status when using <code>--watch</code>. Default is 5 seconds.
    </p>
  </div>
  </div>
</Docs>
